        text="Wessex Archaeology was contracted to carry out an archaeological assessment of geophysical data acquired from aggregate licence Area 507. A number of palaeogeographic features of archaeological potential were identified; these were generally palaeochannel features, both buried and unfilled, potentially associated with the Thames - Medway river system that existed in the region during periods of relatively low sea level between the Cromerian and the Early Holocene. 12 distinct wrecks plus four large pieces of debris were identified.",
