    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="This project concerns the monitoring undertaken during 2005-6 to comply with the conditions of the Food and Environment Protection Act (FEPA) 1985: Part II (as amended), licence reference 31579/02/0 (as amended), issued to NWP Offshore Ltd. for the North Hoyle Offshore Wind Farm. This report represents the second year of post-construction monitoring and the 4th of a 5th year monitoring programme. As the most recent environmental monitoring results are assimilated and compared against those of previous monitoring campaigns at the site, it is now becoming possible to make preliminary conclusions on the overall impact from construction and operation of the wind farm on the physical and biological environment.",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="NWP Offshore Ltd."),
        ]
    ),
    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="This report has been prepared by Subacoustech Ltd for Barrow Offshore Wind Ltd. It describes a series of underwater acoustic measurements undertaken in and around the Barrow Offshore Wind Farm site, on the 30th January and 1st February 2007. The purpose of the measurement programme was to characterise any increase in the ambient subsea noise due to the presence of the operational wind farm, and to assess the range over which any increase in noise occurred.",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="Barrow Offshore Wind Ltd"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="Subacoustech Ltd"),
        ]
    ),
    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="Wessex Archaeology was contracted by Innogy UK Ltd. to undertake an archaeological assessment of 2015 and 2016 geophysical data acquired from the proposed Export Cable Route (ECR) corridor for the Galloper Offshore Wind Farm site. This was undertaken as part of ongoing assessments in advance of the proposed development, and incorporates previous interpretations undertaken by Wessex Archaeology in 2010 and 2015. This report is an amended version after interpretation of the nearshore and final infill data acquisition. Data assessed from the following types of geophysical surveys: sidescan sonar, magnetometer and multibeam echosounder. A total of 603 anomalies have been identified within or impacting on the proposed ECR corridor; fourteen of which have been assigned an A1 discrimination ('anthropogenic origin of archaeological interest'). A total of three historic wreck records of A3 archaeological discrimination exist ('historic record of possible archaeological interest with no corresponding geophysical anomaly'); two of which represent contemporary accounts of recorded losses. A further 586 anomalies of A2 archaeological discrimination ('uncertain origin of possible archaeological interest') have been identified within the ECR corridor.",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="Innogy UK Ltd."),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="Wessex Archaeology"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="procedures", extraction_text="sidescan sonar"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="procedures", extraction_text="magnetometer"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="procedures", extraction_text="multibeam echosounder"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="occurrence records", extraction_text="historic wreck records"),
        ]
    ),
    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="Finfish Survey of Bridlington Bay (August 2011, January and March 2012), in relation to the Inshore Cable Corridor for the Dogger Bank Creyke Beck Projects \r\n\r\nThis survey was designed to evaluate the natural fish ecology, and commercial fisheries utilising gears that are better suited to the capture and retention of species present in the area and such a survey reflects the type of finfish gears used by local fishermen. The results of which provide additional baseline information with regard to the diversity and abundance of species utilising the area which may be affected by the cable laying phase, and which may potentially disrupt the migration of an unknown density of fish during this period. Such an evaluation would assist in determining whether the cable route is important to fish migrations and as a consequence commercial fin fishing.",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="geospatial region", extraction_text="Bridlington Bay"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="projects", extraction_text="Dogger Bank Creyke Beck Projects"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="migratory marine species", extraction_text="fish"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="marine species", extraction_text="Finfish"),
        ]
    ),
    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="2009 South East singlebeam bathymetry dataset from the Channel Coastal Observatory Catalogue (number of records: 700",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="Channel Coastal Observatory"),
        ]
    ),
    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="The purpose of this benthic survey in the Luce Bay was to conduct a targeted survey on the extent, distribution and quality of benthic habitats in the Luce Bay and Sands SAC. A drop-down video survey at 138 locations was undertaken in stages between 10th July and 10th September 2012, to investigate benthic habitats, together with a foot based intertidal survey on 4th August 2012 to map the extent of Sabellaria alveolata reefs. Areas where existing evidence suggested the presence of Modiolus and maerl communities were also investigated. Sampling was also undertaken across the site where no previous seabed data has previously been acquired to enhance the existing knowledge base. A benthic grab survey was undertaken on 9th â?? 10th June 2013 at 16 stations to determine the biotopes of some of the soft sediment areas identified during the drop down camera survey. This survey work in 2012 and 2013 was undertaken by Seastar Survey Ltd, contracted by SNH, from Seastar Survey's own vessel SV Otarie (drop-video) and from a local fishing vessel (grab).",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="Seastar Survey Ltd"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="SNH"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="procedures", extraction_text="foot based intertidal survey"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="procedures", extraction_text="benthic grab survey"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="procedures", extraction_text="drop-down video survey"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="taxon", extraction_text="Sabellaria alveolata"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="taxon", extraction_text="Modiolus"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="ecosystems", extraction_text="benthic habitats"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="geospatial region", extraction_text="Sands SAC"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="geospatial region", extraction_text="Luce Bay"),
        ]
    ),
    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="In accordance with the FEPA licence, there is a requirement to undertake pre-construction and post-construction surveys of a selection of turbine locations and the associated cable corridors to determine rates of scour after construction. Emu Limited was commissioned by Kentish Flats Ltd. to carry out a series of hydrographic surveys spaced at 6 monthly intervals both before and after construction to achieve this requirement.\r\nThis project relates to the seventh such survey, the sixth since construction of the turbine foundations. The fieldwork was performed between 2nd and 5th November 2007 by our subcontractor Port of London Authority (PLA) using the survey vessel Verifier. Depth data were acquired by a multibeam system fully integrated with motion sensor and navigation software.",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="Kentish Flats Ltd."),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="Emu Limited"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="measurements and facts", extraction_text="Depth data"),
        ]
    ),
