    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="Wessex Archaeology (WA) was commissioned by English Heritage (EH) to conduct a project studying the application of geophysical and geotechnical/seabed sampling methodologies to marine aggregate deposits that have been demonstrated to contain potential pre-Devensian or Devensian artefactual material. Artefactual material, including hand axes, flakes, cores and faunal remains, were recovered from dredging licence Area 240 (licensed to Hanson Aggregates Marine Ltd.) in 2008, situated approximately 11km off the coast of Great Yarmouth. The findings show that significant archaeological material can be present in deposits that are being targeted for marine aggregate extraction. The place where the finds were dredged is relatively discrete, and the provenance of the artefacts is secure. The area where the hand axes were recovered is currently subject to a rectangular exclusion zone based on dredger trackplots, implemented voluntarily by Hanson Aggregates Marine Ltd. The principal aim of the project is to improve the future management of the potential effects of aggregate dredging on the marine historic environment by developing techniques to evaluating the source of prehistoric artefactual material discovered in the East Coast region.",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="Hanson Aggregates Marine Ltd."),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="English Heritage"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="geospatial region", extraction_text="Great Yarmouth"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="geospatial region", extraction_text="East Coast region"),
        ]
    ),
    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="The overall objective of the task was to undertake aerial surveys of sea birds within the Dogger Bank windfarm site (Round 3 - Zone 3) within the calendar months from April 2010 to June 2012.\r\n\r\nThe methodology being used for the Forewind contract has been developed by HiDef Aerial Surveying Ltd and is based on aerial surveys using digital imaging equipment. The methodology for video survey of waterbirds was developed by HiDef in conjunction with JNCC. Field trials of this system have demonstrated its ability to meet or exceed the performance requirements specified within the BTO report with current method and protocol directives endorsed by all relevant stake holders including JNCC, SNH, CCW, Natural England, Defra, MFA and The Crown Estate.\r\n\r\nHiDef was contracted to fly surveys focusing on the following areas within Dogger Bank.\r\n\r\nZone - April 2010 to Dec 2010\r\nTranche A - Jan 2011 to Dec 2011\r\nTranche B - July 2011 to Jun 2012\r\n\r\nFor each survey month flown the following are produced.\r\nReport (PDF)\r\nObservations (ESRI shapefile and Excel spreadsheet)\r\nTracks (ESRI shapefile)",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="procedures", extraction_text="aerial surveys"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="geospatial region", extraction_text="Dogger Bank windfarm site"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="marine biodiversity", extraction_text="sea birds"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="Crown Estate"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="Natural England"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="SNH"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="JNCC"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="CCW"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="Defra"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="MFA"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="HiDef Aerial Surveying Ltd"),
        ]
    ),
    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="Benthic survey of the Dogger Bank Tranche A and associated export route. Survey completed by Gardline Environmental on behalf of Forewind Ltd.\r\nThe object of the survey was to investigate pre-selected sites for the presence or absence of Annex I habitats protected under the European Habitats Directive using appropriate guidance notes and high resolution under water video and stills photography (Fresh Water Lens System), to delineate the extent of any Annex I habitat found, also ground truthing of selected sites using a sediment sampler for the determination of Herring Spawning Ground (HSG) potential based on guidelines provided by Cefas (2001). Survey also undertakes characterisation of seabed sediments and Archaeological assessment. \r\n\r\nIn order to accomplish above objectives three methods were used which are: \r\n1)	Fresh Water Lens Camera Procedure\r\n2)	Day Grab Procedure\r\n3)	Mini Hamon Grab Procedure. \r\n	\r\nResults of these methods were provided in field sampling logs (.XLS format) by Gardline Geosurvey Limited. Logs were provided for seabed imagery (deck log + Surveyor log), Day Grab samples (deck log + Surveyor log) and Mini Hamon Grab Samples (deck log + Surveyor log).",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="policies", extraction_text="European Habitats Directive"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="Cefas"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="Gardline Geosurvey Limited"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="Forewind Ltd"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="Gardline Environmental"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="procedures", extraction_text="Mini Hamon Grab Samples"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="procedures", extraction_text="Day Grab Procedure"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="procedures", extraction_text="Fresh Water Lens Camera Procedure"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="procedures", extraction_text="Mini Hamon Grab Procedure"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="geospatial region", extraction_text="Dogger Bank Tranche A"),
        ]
    ),
    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="Review of the data collected for Humber Gateway Limited for metocean. Survey conducted over the period 26th march 2004- 16th Nov 2004 used to characterise the local wave and tidal processes and the manner in which they influence the local sediment regime. The analysis of the data has also used longer-term observations from the neighbouring WaveNet data site at Dowsing, as well as available data from an ABP wave buoy located at Chequer Shoal.\r\n\r\nThese data sets are used together to identify prevailing wave directions and exceedance levels for large waves. Acceptance is based on measurement of local conditions achieving at least a 10% exceedance level in wave height for prevailing directions. seabed mounted acoustic profiler (Nortek AWAC) device has been deployed over a period of seven and a half-month within the HG OWF site. Wave data, collected hourly using a burst period of 512 seconds at 2Hz, Tidal elevations, Tidal velocities, collected in 0.5m vertical bins every 10 minutes using a burst period of 60 seconds, Directional waves, Water samples at service periods, Suspended sediment concentrations from both Optical Back Scatter (OBS)\r\nand Acoustic Back Scatter (ABS) devices. In addition, the local seabed has been characterised by a geophysical survey conducted by Titan in 2004 and with particle size data of surficial sediments from a\r\nbenthic survey conducted by ICES (reported elsewhere). Analysis also includes assessment of the far-field sediment inputs from coastal erosion and freshwater inputs.",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="measurements and facts", extraction_text="particle size data"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="measurements and facts", extraction_text="Tidal velocities"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="geospatial region", extraction_text="Dowsing"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="geospatial region", extraction_text="Chequer Shoal"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="ICES"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="Humber Gateway Limited"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="Titan"),
        ]
    ),
