    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="The project aimed to establish effective methodologies for assessing the fabric, significance and character of English ports and harbours by using a study of those in Cornwall and the Isles of Scilly as a pilot. It involved a rapid assessment of the forces for change affecting Cornwall's ports and harbours and their vulnerability or capability to benefit from change, classifying the sites according to a range of variables, undertaking historic characterisation of selected ports and harbours and carrying out limited field work at the selected sites. Outcomes of the project include a widely disseminated report, a Historic Environment Action Plan (HEAP), management recommendations and a list of those ports and harbours which are candidates for designation.",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="procedures", extraction_text="rapid assessment"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="geospatial region", extraction_text="Cornwall"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="geospatial region", extraction_text="Isles of Scilly"),
        ]
    ),
    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="This file details the Offshore Study Boundary for Project 1 of the Dogger Round 3 windfarm site and links Tranche A to the Onshore Study Boundary and forms the Project 1 Cable Corridor. This area indicates Forewind's area of search for the cable corridor for the first of 12 projects in the Dogger Bank Offshore Wind Farm Zone. The area shown is based on a 1GW grid connection onshore and a desk assessment of known constraints in the area. Further studies will be conducted to narrow down this corridor further although the intention will remain to take the most direct and feasible (in terms of cable engineering) route. This will also be dependent on where exactly, within Tranche A, the first project is sited and hence where the cable will leave the Zone, which is also yet to be decided. Any restrictions to cabling activity in this area could make the project financially unviable due to the large associated costs of cabling.",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="projects", extraction_text="Project 1"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="Forewind"),
        ]
    ),
    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="Centre for Marine and Coastal Studies Ltd (CMACS) were commissioned by West of Duddon\r\nSands Ltd (WoDS) to carry out vessel based surveys of the bird populations in the West of\r\nDuddon Sands offshore wind farm area. The report within this series presents results of the surveys in the West of Duddon Sands field in 2012 which represent the first pre-construction (baseline) survey. Some comments on the results are provided; although the focus of the report is on presentation of the results. Detailed data analysis is being undertaken by NIRAS on behalf of WoDS. Ornithological surveys are planned to continue during the operational phase in accordance with the monitoring schedule and as agreed with the relevant statutory authorities. This series also contains the April - September 2012 bird survey data.",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="marine biodiversity", extraction_text="bird populations"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="West of Duddon  Sands Ltd"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="Centre for Marine and Coastal Studies Ltd"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="NIRAS"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="procedures", extraction_text="vessel based surveys"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="geospatial region", extraction_text="West of Duddon Sands"),
        ]
    ),
    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="The document within this series describes the baseline commercial fishing within areas\r\nrelevant to the proposed Walney and West Duddon Offshore Wind Farms taking\r\naccount of the FEPA, CPA and Defra-CEFAS requirements outlined in the 2004\r\nGuidelines. For the purposes of this assessment, commercial fishing is defined as any\r\nfishing activity legitimately undertaken and declared for tax assessment.\r\nThere is no single data source or recognised model for accurately quantifying the levels\r\nand values of commercial fishing within small discrete sea areas such as the combined\r\nareas of the Walney and West Duddon wind farm sites. Furthermore, the collection and\r\nrecording of national fisheries data by ICES rectangle is primarily for the monitoring\r\nand control of fishing effort and catches over relatively large sea areas, and therefore\r\ninvolves the use of area units for recording data substantially larger than the areas of\r\nwind farms.",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="ICES rectangle"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="policies", extraction_text="CPA"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="policies", extraction_text="2004  Guidelines"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="policies", extraction_text="Defra-CEFAS"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="policies", extraction_text="FEPA"),
        ]
    ),
