    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="This geodatabase contains manually digitised GI created during the Stakmap/Fishermap participatory mapping research project. The geometries have been cleansed and non polygonal features have been converted into polygons using a 300m buffer. The feature classes which contain individual records are CF_activity_individual, CF_additional_individual and CF_club_individual. \r\n One condition of the research was that only those interviewees who explicitly gave permission for their data to be shared would have their own mapping represented in the final product shared with third parties. All other individuals have had their data removed from this feature class. Of 984 interviews, 594 gave their permission for their data to be shared.\r\n Therefore, in addition to the individual records presented in the three feature classes described above, this geodatabase contains a number of summary layers that amalgamate individual interviews onto a standardised grid of 3/4 of a nautical mile longitude and 3/8 of a nautical mile latitude. \r\n \r\n These summary data sets represents the activities of all interviewees, the summarisation process is considered to anonymised the data to a sufficient degree to protect the individual's privacy. As an added measure of protection, data from interviews has only been included in the amalgamated summary/grid layers if the following conditions have been met. \r\n 1) Permission has been granted for the individual data to be used, or\r\n 2) Five or more separate interviews are represented within a single record.",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="projects", extraction_text="Stakmap/Fishermap"),
        ]
    ),
    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="This layer shows the distribution of Wireweed, Sargassum muticum, a non-native species. \r\n This layer forms one of a set of data layers created for the Defra MB0102 contract. This work will support the delivery of a network of Marine Protected Areas as required to meet existing international and national obligations and commitments, including Marine Conservation Zones (MCZs), a new measure to be delivered as part of the Marine and Coastal Access Bill, and equivalent measures under Scottish legislation. The availability of these data layers will also be of importance in underpinning Marine Planning (e.g. licensing) in our marine area.",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="taxon", extraction_text="Wireweed"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="taxon", extraction_text="Sargassum muticum"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="invasive species", extraction_text="Sargassum muticum"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="invasive species", extraction_text="Wireweed"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="projects", extraction_text="Defra MB0102 contract"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="policies", extraction_text="Scottish legislation"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="policies", extraction_text="Marine and Coastal Access Bill"),
        ]
    ),
    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="The North of Celtic Deep rMCZ survey was carried out during 7th – 9th February 2012 on the RV CEFAS Endeavour cruise CEND 03/12. Multibeam bathymetry and backscatter data were collected in between sampling stations. These data are archived with the Marine Environmental Data and Information Network (MEDIN) Data Archive Centres (DACs) including the British Geological Survey (BGS) DAC for geology and geophysics, The Archive for Marine Species and Habitats Data (DASSH) and the United Kingdom Hydrographic Office (UKHO) bathymetry DAC. The full site data package including raw is also available on request from BGS.",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="measurements and facts", extraction_text="Deep"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="British Geological Survey"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="Marine Environmental Data and Information Network"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="Archive for Marine Species and Habitats Data"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="United Kingdom Hydrographic Office"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="procedures", extraction_text="Multibeam bathymetry"),
        ]
    ),
    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="The Firth of Lorn has been selected as a Special Area of Conservation (SAC) for the marine feature â??reefsâ??, an Annex I habitat under the 1992 Habitats Directive. The chief reason for the selection of this site is that the varied physical environment, with its complex group of islands, sounds and inlets characterised by some of the strongest tidal streams in the UK, is reflected in the great variety of reef types and associated communities and species which are amongst the most diverse in both the UK and Europe. The purpose of the current study was to initiate site condition monitoring of the intertidal and subtidal reef habitats within the SAC, establish a baseline biological data set that would facilitate the assessment of the condition of the reef habitats in the future and allow a judgement to be formed on the current condition of these habitats. A hierarchical biological sampling approach was adopted to achieve these aims. An extensive drop-down video survey of subtidal biotopes (habitats and associated species) was undertaken together with more detailed semi-quantitative and quantitative sampling of intertidal and nearshore subtidal reefs and their associated communities.",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="geospatial region", extraction_text="Firth of Lorn"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="geospatial region", extraction_text="UK"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="geospatial region", extraction_text="Europe"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="procedures", extraction_text="drop-down video survey"),
        ]
    ),
    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="This report is concerned with analysis of the 2004 seal survey data, collected during the construction period of the wind farm. The Schedule to Licence states that a monitoring programme for the seals, as agreed with the Sea Mammals Research Unit (SMRU) should be carried out to determine the impact of the wind farm. This is specified in the licence as 2 fly-overs per month at low water for the six summer months (April to September) pre, during and post construction. Data collected prior to construction in 2002 and 2003 were to establish the baseline conditions against which the potential impacts of the wind farm could be measured. The licence states that the data collected during each fly-over should be copied to SMRU and a written report provided to the Licensing Authority at three monthly intervals.",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="Licensing Authority"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="Sea Mammals Research Unit"),
        ]
    ),
    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="A geotechnical survey campaign was undertaken within the vicinity of the Westermost Rough Offshore Wind\r\nFarm. This was supported by a preliminary review of acoustic data and assessment for the presence of Annex I\r\nreefs to minimise the risk of potential damage to protected features.\r\nFollowing the review of existing data, a drop down video survey protocol was\r\ndeveloped (EMU, 2011) and approved by the Marine Management Organisation (MMO). Part of this protocol\r\nidentified that a number of proposed geotechnical sampling sites were likely to be in the vicinity of potential\r\nAnnex I reefs and therefore warranted field ground-truthing by means of drop down video to verify the\r\npresence and status of these features. The video ground-truthing survey has now been completed. Drawing upon the findings of this survey, the 2012 EMU report present within this series provides an update of the assessment of the potential Annex I reefs present at the proposed\r\ngeotechnical sample locations and fulfils condition 3.1.1 of the Marine Licence (Licence L/2011/001075). The aim of the 2013 Fugro EMU document also present within this series was to satisfy Marine Licence condition 31.22 and to address the responses from\r\nthe MMO regarding the Annex I reef features (letter ref: REN024, dated 12th April 2013, and 21st June\r\n2013). The objectives were to assess the impacts (direct and indirect) of the construction activities on\r\nthe potential Annex I features.\r\nThe objectives of this report were to:\r\n? Assess the direct impact (loss of habitat) of each of the construction activities;\r\n? Assess the associated indirect impacts (increase in sediment smothering, and suspended\r\nsediment concentrations); and\r\n? Assess the cumulative impacts of all construction activities.",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="procedures", extraction_text="drop down video survey protocol"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="MMO"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="Marine Management Organisation"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="EMU"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="policies", extraction_text="Marine Licence"),
        ]
    ),
    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="Intertidal sediment infauna and epibiota species abundance data and associated habitat descriptors from a baseline survey of An Grianan lagoon, within the Ulva, Danna and the McCormaig Isles SSSI. The main aims of the survey were to search for lagoon specialist species, to check the condition of the lagoon barrier, and to provide sufficient information for site condition assessment. Some baseline data were also collected for future site condition monitoring.",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="conservation efforts", extraction_text="site condition monitoring"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="geospatial region", extraction_text="Ulva"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="geospatial region", extraction_text="Danna"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="geospatial region", extraction_text="McCormaig Isles SSSI"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="geospatial region", extraction_text="Grianan lagoon"),
        ]
    ),
