    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="This dataset comprises hydrographic data profiles, collected by a conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) sensor package, during July 1996. It incorporates CTD sections between the Inner Hebrides/Scottish mainland and the Outer Hebrides. The data were collected by the Fisheries Research Services Aberdeen Marine Laboratory as part of a large scale hydrographic, chemical and biological survey of the Minches area.",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="geospatial region", extraction_text="Inner Hebrides/Scottish mainland"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="geospatial region", extraction_text="Outer Hebrides"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="Fisheries Research Services Aberdeen Marine Laboratory"),
        ]
    ),
    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="The Lynn and Inner Dowsing (LID) offshore wind farms are comprised of 27 turbines at Lynn and 27 turbines at Inner Dowsing, and are located between 5 km to 8.5 km off the Lincolnshire coast. Construction of the wind farms commenced in 2007 and the wind farms were fully operational by March 2009.\r\nThis annual report, consisting of a Summary Report and Appendices, presents the results of the third and final year of post-construction environmental monitoring at the LID sites, and integrates the results of all previous monitoring to date. The overall purpose of this Summary Report is to fulfil the requirements of the FEPA Licences / Deemed Marine Licences (Lynn Licence 31792/10/1; Inner Dowsing Licence 31814/10/2; and drill arisings FEPA Licence 33553/07/0), which cover the offshore and near shore elements of these projects.\r\nThe LID monitoring programme covers a 10 year period, with some pre-construction surveys commencing in 2002, and the final post-construction survey taking place in 2012. The pre-construction surveys took place between 2002 and 2005, with during-construction surveys being carried out between 2007 and 2008, and the post-construction surveys taking place between 2009 and 2012. Eleven main physical and biological environmental parameters have been monitored during this monitoring programme, including suspended sediment concentrations, currents, beach profiles, subsea noise, fish communities, marine mammals, seabed morphology, ornithology, benthic ecology, archaeology, and drill arisings.",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="measurements and facts", extraction_text="suspended sediment concentrations"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="measurements and facts", extraction_text="beach profiles"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="measurements and facts", extraction_text="currents"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="measurements and facts", extraction_text="subsea noise"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="ecosystems", extraction_text="fish communities"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="geospatial region", extraction_text="Lincolnshire"),
        ]
    ),
    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="As part of JNCC's statutory responsibility to recommend Special Areas of Conservation in the offshore marine area to UK Government, the Marine Protected Sites team needs to gather information to help support these recommendations through collaborative or commissioned survey. On such surveys a variety of data may be recorded using a range of instrumentation. These range from using multibeam echosounders and sidescan sonar to record the bathymetry, seabed texture and morphology through to using high resolution digital video and stills equipment to image the seafloor.\r\n \r\n The data included in this file details hydrographic survey extents for contracts which were commissioned by JNCC and commissioned under the Mapping European Seabed Habitats (MESH) project. For surveyed areas, polygon areas represent actual extents of survey data gathered, for planned surveys the general extent of the area is shown",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="projects", extraction_text="Mapping European Seabed Habitats (MESH) project"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="JNCC"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="Marine Protected Sites team"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="measurements and facts", extraction_text="hydrographic survey extents"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="measurements and facts", extraction_text="bathymetry"),
        ]
    ),
