    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="This Habitats Regulations Assessment addresses the requirement contained in regulation 5(2)(g) of the Infrastructure Planning Regulations 2009, which requires an applicant for development consent to provide a report identifying any European Site to which regulation 61 of the Conservation Regulations 2010 applies, or any Ramsar site, which may be affected by the proposed development, together with sufficient information that will enable the Competent Authority to make an appropriate assessment of the implications for the site if required by regulation 61(1). The offshore wind farm componenet of the proposed development is not located within a European or Ramsar site but the offshore cable corridor crosses the Liverpool Bay SPA site abd the Morecambe Bay SAC, SPA and Ramsar sites to make landfall on the Lancastrian coast, south of Heysham. The Project is not directly connected with or necessary to the management of these sites or any of the European or Ramsar sites considered in this assessment.",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="geospatial region", extraction_text="Liverpool Bay"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="geospatial region", extraction_text="Lancastrian coast"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="geospatial region", extraction_text="European Site"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="geospatial region", extraction_text="Heysham"),
        ]
    ),
    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="This study forms chapters (9 &amp; 10) of the Stage 2 Preliminary Environmental Information (Stage 2 PEI) of the Rhiannon Offshore Wind Farm, which is part of the Environmental Impact Assessment (EIA). \r\nThe study was carried out by CMACS - Centre for Marine &amp; Coastal Studies and it describes the existing environment with regards to Benthic Ecology and Fish and Shellfish Ecology and assesses the potential impacts of the Offshore Development area of the proposed Rhiannon Wind Farm (RWF) on the Benthic and Fish ecology.\r\nThe assessment describes and focuses on the impacts on relevant receptors associated with the Offshore Development of Rhiannon Wind Farm (RWF), which extends seaward from Mean High Water Springs (MHWS) seaward (including any potential impacts in the intertidal area). This consists of the Wind Farm Site and Export Cable Area (ECA – which is the area within which sub-sea export cables will bring power from the Wind farm site to shore at a number of potential Cable Landfall Sites along the north Anglesey coastline). The Wind Farm Site includes all wind turbines, intra-array cables, and ancillary structures such as substations and convertor stations. The Potential cumulative impacts between the Offshore and Onshore developments was also assessed.\r\n\r\nCorresponding Centrica Document No: \r\nBenthic Ecology :SE-D-EV-075-0002-000000-009 ; SE-D-EV-075-0002-000000-009-Att1; SE-D-EV-075-0002-000000-009-Att2; SE-D-EV-075-0002-000000-009-Att3; \r\nIntertidal Technical Report: SE-D-EV-075-0002-000000-009-Att4; \r\nFish and Shellfish Ecology : SE-D-EV-075-0002-000000-010; \r\n\r\nAvailable Datasets : 1. ArcGIS files (mxds, .gdb, shapefiles, metadata files (xml)), 2. Drawings (pdf, jpeg), 	3. Reports (.doc, .xls, .txt)\r\n\r\nPlease note reports are still in draft.",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="CMACS"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="marine biodiversity", extraction_text="Benthic Ecology"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="migratory marine species", extraction_text="Fish"),
        ]
    ),
