    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="This geodatabase contains manually digitised GI created during the Stakmap/Fishermap participatory mapping research project. The geometries have been cleansed and non polygonal features have been converted into polygons using a 300m buffer. \r\n This feature class records the number of divers involved in spearfishing and hand gathering food on a monthly basis. The month fields record the number of interviewees that have contributed to this data, the fields with a count suffix record the number of individuals. Individual records have been summarised onto a grid 3/4 nautical mile longitude by 3/8 nautical mile latitude.\r\n This summary data set represents the activities of all interviewees, the summarisation process is considered to anonymised the data to a sufficient degree to protect the individual's privacy. As an added measure of protection, data from interviews has only been included in the amalgamated summary/grid layers if the following conditions have been met. \r\n 1) Permission has been granted for the individual data to be used, or\r\n 2) Five or more separate interviews are represented within a single record.",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="projects", extraction_text="Stakmap/Fishermap"),
        ]
    ),
    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="This Aquatic Survey and Monitoring Limited (ASML) project was commissioned to assess the interest feature - Reefs (subtidal), within the cSAC, by surveying several sub-features of Lundy's reefs, identified as ecologically important components. These components, outlined in the regulation 33 package, include; kelp forest communities, subtidal bedrock and stable boulder communities and Eunicella (Pink Sea Fan) characterised reef, all to be surveyed by 'drop-down video' in order to establish a baseline, from which in the future, an assessment of the target; 'No decrease in the distribution, extent and range of biotopes from a baseline' will be made. Some biotopes and other structural aspects of these same components were also to be surveyed by quantitative diving techniques, to establish a baseline against which an assessment of the target, 'Species composition: no significant deviation from baseline' will be made.",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="ecosystems", extraction_text="kelp forest communities"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="policies", extraction_text="regulation 33 package"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="procedures", extraction_text="drop-down video"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="procedures", extraction_text="quantitative diving techniques"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="cSAC"),
        ]
    ),
    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="CONFIDENTIAL - INFORMATION ABOUT BATS ETC. Lapwings Consultants Ltd has been commissioned by Centrica, through RPS\r\nGroup, to undertake ecological surveys along the corridor of a proposed\r\nelectricity cable taking power from off-shore wind farms to a new sub-station\r\nnear Walpole St Andrew. The scope of the ecological surveys was to identify\r\nthe use made of the study area by badgers, otters, water voles, spined loach,\r\ngreat crested newts, reptiles, foraging bats, the farmland breeding bird\r\ncommunity, breeding waders on the saltmarsh, and to determine if any\r\nhedgerows are of nature conservation importance. The surveys were\r\nundertaken in the period mid-May to mid-July and early-mid September 2006.\r\nThis series contains a report which presents the results of the surveys and makes an assessment of\r\nnature conservation interest of the site for the groups concerned, and\r\nexamines potential impacts from, and mitigation for, the proposed cable\r\ninstallation and sub-station construction. A separate document detailing features of importance for nature conservation in the Wash, and relevant designations, is also provided. In addition, phase 1 habitat survey data is provided, showing details of habitat types and boundary features around the proposed onshore cable route development area.",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="ecosystems", extraction_text="saltmarsh"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="geospatial region", extraction_text="Walpole St Andrew"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="Lapwings Consultants Ltd"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="Centrica"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="RPS  Group"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="marine species", extraction_text="spined loach"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="marine species", extraction_text="great crested newts"),
        ]
    ),
