        text="This dataset comprises hydrographic data profiles, collected by a conductivity-temperature-depth (CTD) sensor package, during September 1986. It incorporates CTD sections across the North Channel, an extensive grid of stations in the Firth of Clyde, sections from Islay to Northern Ireland, westwards from Islay, from Jura to Mull, westwards from Mull and from the Sound of Mull to Barra Head. The data were collected by the Scottish Marine Biological Association.",
