    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="Following identification of areas of Annex I habitat within the greater Thames Area of Search (AoS), this report \r\n gives a brief outline of two sites within the AoS which are considered appropriate for designation as SACs. \r\n These are: \r\n â?¢ Margate Sands; and \r\n â?¢ Long Sands. \r\n This report has been produced for the purpose of providing Natural England with summary information regarding \r\n the characteristics of these sites. For each site, an initial assessment against the Habitats Directive Annex III Stage \r\n 1A site selection criteria has been made, and is presented together with a brief description of the site and its \r\n features. This report is not intended to represent a complete site selection report. Following selection of one (or \r\n both) of these sites by Natural England, a full site selection report will be prepared. This later report will contain a \r\n more detailed assessment of the site against the site selection criteria and guiding principles, along with full \r\n supporting scientific evidence.",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="Natural England"),
        ]
    ),
    lx.data.ExampleData(
        text="The purpose of this benthic survey (cruise 1012S) south-west of the island of Islay was to improve knowledge of the occurrence and distribution of species and habitats of recognised conservation importance, particularly priority marine features (PMFs), because this area is one of the sites of interest to the development of marine renewables. The installation of tidal energy devices off Islay was proposed at the time of this survey. A further aim was to assess the implications of this planned renewable energy development on the features of importance. An underwater video survey were conducted by MSS for MSS on the 18-31st August 2012 to collect detailed biological information on the seabed species and habitat features present. Drop-down video drift tows were undertaken at 40 sites. Analyses on the seabed video and still photographic imagery, commissioned by SNH, were used to describe the nature of the seabed in terms of the physical structure and the species assemblages. MSS used the vessel FRV Scotia for this survey.",
        extractions=[
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="geospatial region", extraction_text="Islay"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="SNH"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="organizations", extraction_text="MSS"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="taxon", extraction_text="species"),
            lx.data.Extraction(extraction_class="procedures", extraction_text="underwater video survey"),
        ]
    ),
